[TestSeriesVMCheck/step_from_group_params - 1]
- description: step from group params
  content: |
    - name: g
      params:
        step: ["10m"]
      rules:
      - record: foo:sum
        expr: sum(foo) offset 1h
  output: |
    6 |     expr: sum(foo) offset 1h
                      ^^^
                      `foo` had 14 pauses of at least 10m in the last 1w on `prom` VictoriaMetrics server at
                      https://simple.example.com, the longest at least 1h. vmalert evaluates this rule with
                      instant queries that look back 10m, the query step from `params` of its group (10m),
                      so evaluations during these pauses see no `foo`.
  problem:
    reporter: promql/series
    summary: pauses between samples longer than the query lookback
    details: |-
        vmalert evaluates rules with instant queries. For a selector without a lookbehind window VictoriaMetrics returns the last sample within the query step before the evaluation time, `-datasource.queryStep` of vmalert (5m by default) or `step` from the group `params`. During pauses between samples longer than that the selector returns nothing: a firing alert resolves and its `for` starts again when the metric is back, a recording rule writes no sample. Graphs and pint range queries don't show such pauses, VictoriaMetrics range queries look back about the usual interval between samples.

        Pauses at least once a day on average are usually how the metric is written: stream aggregation outputs, batch jobs, or a scrape interval longer than the query step. To use the last sample of such a metric read it with `last_over_time(selector[window])` and a window longer than the longest normal pause. pint measured the pauses with `count(count_over_time(selector[step]))` over the last 1w.
    diagnostics:
        - message: '`foo` had 14 pauses of at least 10m in the last 1w on `prom` VictoriaMetrics server at https://simple.example.com, the longest at least 1h. vmalert evaluates this rule with instant queries that look back 10m, the query step from `params` of its group (10m), so evaluations during these pauses see no `foo`.'
          firstcolumn: 5
          lastcolumn: 7
          kind: 0
    lines:
        first: 6
        last: 6
    severity: 1
    anchor: 0

